IMPORT prelude

-- Mississippi Code of 1972, Title 27, chapter 7 (income tax): what a resident individual owes. The rates (s 27-7-5, as
-- amended by House Bill 1 of 2025, the "Build Up Mississippi Act", and its Section 2 for 2031 on); the personal and
-- additional exemptions (s 27-7-21); the optional standard deduction (s 27-7-17(3)(b)).
--
-- SEAT: the individual Mississippi resident (or the married couple living together) who asks "How much Mississippi income
-- tax do I owe on my taxable income?". The Legislative Budget Office's and the commissioner's figures that drive the
-- reductions from 2031 are encoded for what they mean to that person: a reduction in effect for the year, asked as a fact.
--
-- Edition and sources. The official Code is published under contract by LexisNexis and was not used (its public access
-- platform presents a CAPTCHA; the Secretary of State asserts copyright: see ../../SOURCE-LICENSE.md). The text comes from
-- the Legislature's own bill documents, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/:
--   ms-2025-hb1-build-up-mississippi-act-as-sent-to-governor.txt (enacted; approved 27 March 2025) for s 27-7-5;
--   ms-2026-hb1996-introduced-brings-forward-27-7-21.txt (a bill that died, which "brought forward" s 27-7-21 unchanged);
--   ms-2026-hb0866-introduced-brings-forward-27-7-17.txt (likewise for s 27-7-17).
-- Each reprint is the section as it stood when the bill was introduced; the Legislature's code-section indexes show no
-- enacted amendment since (NOTES.md finding 4 on how far that can be trusted).
--
-- Gross income, the business deductions and the itemized deductions (ss 27-7-15, 27-7-17(1), (3)(a)) are taken as facts.
--
-- NOT ENCODED (answers `not covered` where a question can reach it): nonresidents and part-year residents (s 27-7-21(i),
-- s 27-7-17(3)(c)); taxable years before 2024; fiscal years spanning a rate change (s 27-7-5(4)); estates, trusts and
-- corporations; credits; withholding and filing (not deposited).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Mississippi individual income tax`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `a nonresident or part-year resident is not encoded (s 27-7-21(i), s 27-7-17(3)(c))`
    `only calendar years 2024 and later are encoded`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

DECLARE `Filing status` IS ONE OF
    `single`
    `married filing a joint or combined return`
    `married filing separate returns`
    `head of family`

GIVEN `text` IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Filing status`
`the filing status named` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `text` EQUALS "married filing jointly" THEN `married filing a joint or combined return`
        IF `text` EQUALS "married filing separately" THEN `married filing separate returns`
        IF `text` EQUALS "head of family" THEN `head of family`
        OTHERWISE `single`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER, `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS IF `x` AT LEAST `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

§§ `s 27-7-5 -- the rates`

-- s 27-7-5(1)(a)(i)6: "For calendar year 2022 and all taxable years thereafter, there shall be no tax levied on the first
-- Five Thousand Dollars ($5,000.00) of taxable income"; (1)(b)(i): "For calendar year 2023 and all calendar years
-- thereafter, there shall be no tax levied" on taxable income from $5,000 to $10,000; (1)(b)(ii): on all taxable income over
-- $10,000: 4.7% for 2024, 4.4% for 2025, 4% for 2026, 3.75% for 2027, 3.5% for 2028, 3.25% for 2029, and "For calendar year
-- 2030 and all calendar years thereafter, except as otherwise provided in Section 2 of this act, ... three percent (3%)".
-- HB 1 (2025), Section 2(2): for 2031 and later, if the Working Cash-Stabilization Reserve Fund is fully funded and revenue
-- exceeds appropriations by enough, "the tax ... shall be reduced by" 0.2%, 0.25% or 0.3%; (4): at 0% the tax "shall be
-- eliminated". Whether a reduction applies depends on figures the Legislative Budget Office and the commissioner provide;
-- the total reduction in effect for the year is asked as a fact, read as percentage points off the 3% rate (NOTES.md
-- finding 2).
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER
      `Section 2 reduction in effect, in percentage points` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rate on taxable income over $10,000` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `calendar year` EQUALS 2024 THEN 4.7%
        IF `calendar year` EQUALS 2025 THEN 4.4%
        IF `calendar year` EQUALS 2026 THEN 4%
        IF `calendar year` EQUALS 2027 THEN 3.75%
        IF `calendar year` EQUALS 2028 THEN 3.5%
        IF `calendar year` EQUALS 2029 THEN 3.25%
        IF `calendar year` EQUALS 2030 THEN 3%
        OTHERWISE `the larger of` 0 (3% MINUS (`Section 2 reduction in effect, in percentage points` DIVIDED BY 100))

GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER
      `taxable income` IS A NUMBER
      `Section 2 reduction in effect, in percentage points` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax under s 27-7-5` MEANS
    (`the rate on taxable income over $10,000` `calendar year` `Section 2 reduction in effect, in percentage points`)
        TIMES (`the larger of` 0 (`taxable income` MINUS 10000))

§§ `s 27-7-21 -- exemptions`

-- (b) single: $6,000; (c) "married individuals living together, a joint personal exemption of ... Twelve Thousand Dollars
-- ($12,000.00)"; (d) head of family: $9,500, and the head of family gets the dependent exemption "only to the extent of
-- dependents in excess of the one (1) dependent needed to qualify"; (e) $1,500 for each s 152 dependent "other than husband
-- or wife"; (f) $1,500 for a taxpayer or spouse aged 65 or more; (g) $1,500 for a taxpayer or spouse who is blind; (h) on
-- separate returns by a husband and wife "the personal and additional exemptions ... shall be divided equally between the
-- spouses".
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
      `dependents` IS A NUMBER
      `taxpayer and spouse aged 65 or more` IS A NUMBER
      `taxpayer and spouse blind` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the exemptions under s 27-7-21` MEANS
    CONSIDER `status`
    WHEN `single` THEN 6000 PLUS `additional`
    WHEN `head of family` THEN 9500 PLUS (1500 TIMES (`the larger of` 0 (`dependents` MINUS 1))) PLUS `age and blindness`
    WHEN `married filing a joint or combined return` THEN 12000 PLUS `additional`
    WHEN `married filing separate returns` THEN (12000 PLUS `additional`) DIVIDED BY 2
    WHERE
        `age and blindness` MEANS 1500 TIMES (`taxpayer and spouse aged 65 or more` PLUS `taxpayer and spouse blind`)
        `additional` MEANS (1500 TIMES `dependents`) PLUS `age and blindness`

@export How much may I deduct for personal and additional exemptions on my Mississippi return (s 27-7-21)?
GIVEN `filing status` IS A STRING @desc Your filing status. One of: "single", "married filing jointly" (married and living together, joint or combined return), "married filing separately", "head of family"
      `dependents` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependents (IRC s 152, not your spouse) you claim; for married people filing separately, the couple's total
      `aged 65 or more` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of you (you, and your spouse if married) were 65 or older before the end of the year
      `blind` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of you (you, and your spouse if married) were blind at the end of the year
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much may I deduct for exemptions` MEANS
    `the exemptions under s 27-7-21` (`the filing status named` `filing status`) `dependents` `aged 65 or more` `blind`

§§ `s 27-7-17(3)(b) -- the standard deduction`

-- "In lieu of the individual nonbusiness itemized deductions ..., an optional standard deduction of: (i) ... Four Thousand
-- Six Hundred Dollars ($4,600.00) for each calendar year thereafter in the case of married individuals filing a joint or
-- combined return; (ii) ... Two Thousand Three Hundred Dollars ($2,300.00) for each calendar year thereafter in the case of
-- married individuals filing separate returns; (iii) Three Thousand Four Hundred Dollars ($3,400.00) in the case of a head
-- of family; or (iv) Two Thousand Three Hundred Dollars ($2,300.00) in the case of an individual who is not married."
-- "In the case of separate returns by a husband and wife, the standard deduction shall not be allowed to either if the
-- taxable income of one of the spouses is determined without regard to the standard deduction."
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
      `my spouse itemizes on a separate return` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the optional standard deduction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `status`
    WHEN `married filing a joint or combined return` THEN 4600
    WHEN `married filing separate returns` THEN IF `my spouse itemizes on a separate return` THEN 0 ELSE 2300
    WHEN `head of family` THEN 3400
    WHEN `single` THEN 2300

@export What is my Mississippi optional standard deduction (s 27-7-17(3)(b))?
GIVEN `filing status` IS A STRING @desc Your filing status. One of: "single", "married filing jointly", "married filing separately", "head of family"
      `spouse itemizes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Married filing separately only: whether your spouse itemizes deductions instead of taking the standard deduction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my standard deduction` MEANS
    `the optional standard deduction` (`the filing status named` `filing status`) `spouse itemizes`

§§ `Questions for the taxpayer`

DECLARE `My Mississippi tax` HAS
    `deduction`        IS A NUMBER
    `exemptions`       IS A NUMBER
    `taxable income`   IS A NUMBER
    `income tax`       IS A NUMBER

@export How much Mississippi income tax do I owe for the year as a resident (ss 27-7-5, 27-7-17, 27-7-21), before credits and withholding?
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year of the return (2024 or later)
      `resident all year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a Mississippi resident for the whole year
      `filing status` IS A STRING @desc Your filing status. One of: "single", "married filing jointly", "married filing separately", "head of family"
      `income after business deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Mississippi gross income for the year less the business deductions of s 27-7-17(1) (and, if married filing separately, your own share), in US dollars
      `itemizes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you itemize your nonbusiness deductions instead of taking the standard deduction
      `itemized deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc If you itemize: your Mississippi individual nonbusiness itemized deductions (s 27-7-17(3)(a)), in US dollars; else 0
      `spouse itemizes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Married filing separately only: whether your spouse itemizes
      `dependents` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependents (IRC s 152, not your spouse) you claim; for married people filing separately, the couple's total
      `aged 65 or more` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of you (you, and your spouse if married) were 65 or older before the end of the year
      `blind` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of you (you, and your spouse if married) were blind at the end of the year
      `reduction from 2031` IS A NUMBER @desc For 2031 and later only: the total reduction, in percentage points, of the 3% rate in effect under Section 2 of House Bill 1 (2025) (for example 0.2); 0 if none or before 2031
GIVETH AN `Answer` `My Mississippi tax`
`How much Mississippi income tax do I owe` MEANS
    IF (NOT `resident all year`)
    THEN `not covered` `a nonresident or part-year resident is not encoded (s 27-7-21(i), s 27-7-17(3)(c))`
    ELSE IF `calendar year` LESS THAN 2024
         THEN `not covered` `only calendar years 2024 and later are encoded`
         ELSE `answered` (`My Mississippi tax` WITH
                `deduction`      IS `the deduction`
                `exemptions`     IS `the exemptions`
                `taxable income` IS `the taxable income`
                `income tax`     IS `the tax under s 27-7-5` `calendar year` `the taxable income` `reduction from 2031`)
    WHERE
        `status` MEANS `the filing status named` `filing status`
        `the deduction` MEANS
            IF `itemizes` THEN `itemized deductions` ELSE `the optional standard deduction` `status` `spouse itemizes`
        `the exemptions` MEANS `the exemptions under s 27-7-21` `status` `dependents` `aged 65 or more` `blind`
        `the taxable income` MEANS `the larger of` 0 ((`income after business deductions` MINUS `the deduction`) MINUS `the exemptions`)

@export How much Mississippi income tax is charged on a taxable income for a calendar year (s 27-7-5; HB 1 of 2025)?
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year (2024 or later)
      `taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Mississippi taxable income, in US dollars
      `reduction from 2031` IS A NUMBER @desc For 2031 and later only: the total reduction, in percentage points, in effect under Section 2 of House Bill 1 (2025); 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What tax is charged on my taxable income` MEANS
    `the tax under s 27-7-5` `calendar year` `taxable income` `reduction from 2031`
